/* rawtext — the verbatim literal <<…>> under load.

   The job: carry a fenced Cufet sample whose own code uses raw literals,
   so the outer literal must nest — inner << >> pairs stay in the content
   by depth counting. Quotes, braces, backslashes and {holes} all arrive
   verbatim: no escapes, no interpolation, no meta-sequence at all.

   The checks print PASS/FAIL so the harness can assert on them.
   The one documented limitation (a lone >> closes early) is why every
   angle-bracket pair in the content is balanced. */

Bind void to play:
    Define sample as <<
Define path as <<C:\Users\me>>.
Define doc as <<{"name": "rabbit", "gift": "fire"}>>.
State "the {hole} stays literal".
>>.

    State "--- the sample, fenced ---".
    State "```".
    State sample.
    State "```".
    State "".

    State "--- checks ---".
    If sample contains <<C:\Users\me>>, state "inner literal survived nesting: PASS".
    Otherwise, state "inner literal survived nesting: FAIL".

    If sample contains <<{"name": "rabbit", "gift": "fire"}>>:
        State "json arrived verbatim (braces and quotes): PASS".
    Done.
    Otherwise, state "json arrived verbatim (braces and quotes): FAIL".

    If sample contains <<{hole}>>, state "braces stayed literal (no interpolation): PASS".
    Otherwise, state "braces stayed literal (no interpolation): FAIL".

    Define lines as (sample trimmed) split by "\n".
    If the number of lines is 3, state "multiline content counted 3 lines: PASS".
    Otherwise, state "multiline content counted 3 lines: FAIL".

    Define empty as <<>>.
    If the length of empty is 0, state "empty raw literal is empty: PASS".
    Otherwise, state "empty raw literal is empty: FAIL".

    If <<a"b>> is "a\"b", state "raw and escaped forms agree on value: PASS".
    Otherwise, state "raw and escaped forms agree on value: FAIL".

    Define name as "kick_".
    State <<concat idiom: >> joined to (<<C:\Users\>> joined to name).
Done.

Cast play.